# Cursor Configuration for Pimpa-Raka Game Project

# This file configures Cursor to automatically reference the project framework documentation
# for all development tasks to ensure consistency with established patterns and conventions.

# Framework Documentation Reference
# CRITICAL: Always reference PROJECT_FRAMEWORK_DOCUMENTATION.md before making any changes
# This document contains the complete framework architecture, patterns, and conventions.

# Project Context
# This is a 2D platformer game built in Godot 4.3 with:
# - State machine architecture for entity behaviors
# - Room-based level system with dynamic loading
# - Player movement system with advanced platformer mechanics
# - Health/life system with respawn mechanics
# - Smart camera system with room boundaries
# - Collectible system with modular items
# - Color palette system for pixel art

# Key Systems to Always Consider:
# - RoomManager: Handles room loading, transitions, and player spawning
# - HealthManager: Manages lives, damage, death, and respawn
# - GameStateManager: Game-wide state management (playing, paused, game over)
# - State Machine System: Clean entity behaviors with State/StateMachine pattern
# - SmartCamera: Room-aware camera that follows player within boundaries
# - GameColors: Centralized color palette with 15 colors from retro-saffron palette

# Development Guidelines:
# 1. Always read PROJECT_FRAMEWORK_DOCUMENTATION.md before making changes
# 2. Follow established naming conventions and file organization
# 3. Use existing patterns for new features (states, rooms, collectibles)
# 4. Maintain consistency with the state machine architecture
# 5. Integrate properly with the room management system
# 6. Use the color palette system for all visual elements

# When creating new rooms:
# - Copy Room0.tscn as template
# - Add required nodes (PlayerSpawn, TileMapLayer, Doors)
# - Register in RoomManager.setup_rooms()
# - Set up room transitions in door nodes

# When creating new states:
# - Extend State class
# - Implement enter(), exit(), update(), physics_update()
# - Add to StateMachine as child node
# - Set up transitions in check_transitions()

# When creating new collectibles:
# - Extend Collectible class
# - Override collect() method for custom behavior
# - Set up scene with Area2D and collision shape

# Color Palette Usage:
# - Access colors via GameColors.COLOR_NAME
# - Use GameColors.get_color_by_name() for dynamic access
# - Get categories via GameColors.get_*_colors()

# File Organization:
# - Scripts organized by system/functionality
# - Scenes organized by entity type
# - Resources centralized in resources/ folder

# Naming Conventions:
# - States: EntityState (e.g., PlayerIdleState)
# - Managers: EntityManager (e.g., RoomManager)
# - Components: EntityComponent (e.g., MovementComponent)
# - Rooms: RoomX.tscn where X is room number
# - Scenes: PascalCase (e.g., Player.tscn)

# Signal Usage:
# - State transitions: transition_requested signal
# - Health changes: health_changed signal
# - Room changes: room_changed signal
# - Game state: game_state_changed signal

# Singleton Access:
# - RoomManager: get_node("/root/RoomManager")
# - HealthManager: get_node("/root/HealthManager")
# - GameStateManager: get_node("/root/GameStateManager")

# CRITICAL: Always reference PROJECT_FRAMEWORK_DOCUMENTATION.md for complete details
